<title>USA: Chase chargeoff rate seen up in first half.</title>
<headline>Chase chargeoff rate seen up in first half.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Credit card net chargeoffs could climb in the first half of 1997 before stabilizing in the second half, Chase Manhattan Corp's Chief Financial Officer Peter Tobin said.</p>
<p>&quot;We do expect to see some uptick in chargeoff rates in the first half and then probably in the second half some levelling off,&quot; he said on a conference call.</p>
<p>Chase reported a fourth quarter credit card chargeoff rate of 5.11 percent of managed receivables compared to 4.95 percent in the third quarter.</p>
</text>
